stage: 3
finding: P2: The promised tests do not reject incorrectly drawn hulls/triangle meshes. In shape-mesh.test.ts verify(), winding is checked only against the returned normal; shape-mesh.ts triangle() derives that normal from the same vertex ordering. Reversing every hull/mesh triangle therefore reverses both winding and normals and still passes every assertion, although back-face culling and lighting draw the wrong side. Surface/bounds checks also do not prove face coverage: dropping box faces while retaining vertices on opposite faces can pass. The reflected mesh fixture checks only z=0, not the expected outward normal or triangle orientation. Smallest fix: assert independent expected outward normals/orientation for hull faces and the clockwise/reflected mesh fixture, and expected face/triangle coverage (or surface area) for these known fixtures; verify reversal and missing-face controls fail. Implementation presently produces the same cube surface positions/normals and 12 triangles as the old cube, independently checked; this finding is about the explicit stage proof, not a demonstrated current Box Stack visual regression.
